WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:08.119
One marketplace merchant, merchant 7, has 30 percent of a million payments.

2
00:00:08.119 --> 00:00:14.404
To join payments with merchants, Spark shuffles both into 16 partitions by merchant id.

3
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.262
Every row with the same key goes to the same partition.

4
00:00:18.262 --> 00:00:21.525
So all of merchant 7's payments land in one task.

5
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.857
The median task fetches about 44 thousand records.

6
00:00:25.857 --> 00:00:30.097
That one fetches 346 thousand, eight times as many.

7
00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:33.046
A stage ends when its slowest task ends.

8
00:00:33.046 --> 00:00:36.103
Fifteen cores finish early and wait for one.

9
00:00:36.103 --> 00:00:37.007
This is skew.

10
00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.212
More partitions don't help.

11
00:00:39.212 --> 00:00:45.649
Merchant 7 is one key, and one key lands in one partition, out of 16 or out of 2,000.

12
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:48.854
Adaptive query execution waits for the shuffle.

13
00:00:48.854 --> 00:00:53.112
When the map tasks finish, Spark knows the size of every partition.

14
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:59.971
A partition more than five times the median, and over 256 megabytes, counts as skewed.

15
00:00:59.971 --> 00:01:05.324
AQE splits it, and gives each piece its own copy of merchant 7's row.

16
00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:09.293
It can only cut between the blocks the map tasks wrote.

17
00:01:09.293 --> 00:01:16.469
Four map tasks make at most four pieces: 16 tasks become 19, and the hottest fetches a quarter of before.

18
00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:18.850
Salting splits the key by hand.

19
00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:27.719
Each payment gets a salt from 0 to 7, taken from its payment id, and each merchant row is copied eight times, once per salt.

20
00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:34.117
Joined on merchant and salt, merchant 7 becomes eight keys that hash to different tasks.

21
00:01:34.117 --> 00:01:37.437
The hottest task drops to 126 thousand records.

22
00:01:37.437 --> 00:01:39.909
Some salts still share a partition.

23
00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.866
Take the salt from the data, never at random.

24
00:01:42.866 --> 00:01:47.035
A retried task must send every row where the first attempt sent it.

25
00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:50.379
One hot key makes one task do the work of many.

26
00:01:50.379 --> 00:01:52.763
Split the key, and the work spreads.
